selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#submodules\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Submodules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#submodules\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"../ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Duct hydraulics shared by cooling channels, piping and manifolds.</p><p>This subpackage contains shared path geometry, explicit pipe hydraulics,\nannular ducts, orifices and orifice plates, and volute and collector manifolds. It depends only on <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../common/index.html#module-pyskyfire.common\" title=\"pyskyfire.common\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common</span></code></a> for\nplanar section primitives and friction correlations and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../thermo/index.html#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo</span></code></a> for fluid state records,\nand it does not import from <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../regen/index.html#module-pyskyfire.regen\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen</span></code></a> or <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../network/index.html#module-pyskyfire.network\" title=\"pyskyfire.network\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network</span></code></a>,\nso cooling channels, turbopump hardware and engine-network adapters can all\ndepend on it without a cycle.</p>", "a[href=\"injector/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.injector.injector<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.injector.injector\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>An injector: sets of elements placed on the face, and the flow through them.</p><p>An <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"injector/Injector.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Injector</span></code></a> is a list of <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"injector/ElementSet.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.ElementSet\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.ElementSet\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ElementSet</span></code></a> objects. Each set is one\nelement type repeated at positions the user supplies as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(r,</span> <span class=\"pre\">\u03b8)</span></code> arrays,\nhowever they were found. The injector holds no face outline or keep-out\nregions: the positions are the only record of where elements are, and\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"injector/Injector.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector.checks\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector.checks\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Injector.checks()</span></code></a> reports what the injector itself can check.</p>", "a[href=\"impinging/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.injector.impinging<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.injector.impinging\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Impinging elements: jets drilled so that they meet at one point.</p><p>An impinging element is a set of jets aimed at a common impingement point a\nheight above the face. Like and unlike doublets, triplets and pentads are the\nsame class with different jets: a like doublet has two jets on one feed, an\nunlike doublet one on each, an O-F-O triplet a fuel jet on the axis between two\noxidizer jets. Each jet\u2019s inclination is its own, so an unlike doublet can\nlean its jets unequally to point the resultant momentum down the axis.</p>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.injector\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.injector<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.injector\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Injectors: element sets on a face, and the flow from each feed through them.</p><p>Each element type is its own class. <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ImpingingElement</span></code> is the first:\njets aimed at a common point, which covers like and unlike doublets, triplets\nand pentads. Holes are <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice</span></code> objects, so sizing,\ndischarge coefficients, choking and cavitation come from <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts</span></code></a>.\nThis subpackage depends on <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts</span></code></a> and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../thermo/index.html#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo</span></code></a>\nonly; the engine network adapts it through\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorBlock</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"../thermo/index.html#module-pyskyfire.thermo\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Fluid properties, thermodynamic states and combustion-gas aerothermodynamics.</p><p>CEA-backed APIs are loaded on first access so fluid and nozzle-loss utilities\ncan be imported without loading CEA, including through the package root.</p>", "a[href=\"element/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.injector.element<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.injector.element\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>What every injector element type offers the injector it sits in.</p><p>An element is one repeated unit on the faceplate: an impinging doublet, a\ncoaxial swirl element, a pintle. Each type has its own class, its own\nparameters and its own modelling. The injector asks each of them only two\nthings: where its holes are and which feed supplies each one\n(<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"element/Element.html#pyskyfire.injector.element.Element.holes\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.element.Element.holes\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Element.holes()</span></code></a>), and what its flows mean for mixing\n(<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"element/Element.html#pyskyfire.injector.element.Element.diagnostics\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.element.Element.diagnostics\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Element.diagnostics()</span></code></a>).</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
